core, classification_report\n\n# Initialize the baseline classifier\ndummy_clf = DummyClassifier(strategy=\"most_frequent\")\n\n# Train the classifier\ndummy_clf.fit(X_train, y_train)\n\n# Predict the validation set\ny_pred_dummy = dummy_clf.predict(X_val)\n\n# Evaluate the predictions\nprint(\"Accuracy:\", accuracy_score(y_val, y_pred_dummy))\nprint(classification_report(y_val, y_pred_dummy))","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-21T12:39:28.216369Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-21T12:39:28.216755Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-21T12:39:28.237588Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-21T12:39:28.216712Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-21T12:39:28.23672Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Accuracy: 0.5705843729481287\n              precision    recall  f1-score   support\n\n           0       0.57      1.00      0.73       869\n           1       0.00      0.00      0.00       654\n\n    accuracy                           0.57      1523\n   macro avg       0.29      0.50      0.36      1523\nweighted avg       0.33      0.57      0.41      1523\n\n","output_type":"stream"},{"name":"stderr","text":"/usr/local/lib/python3.13/dist-packages/sklearn/metrics/_classification.py:1565: UndefinedMetricWarning: Precision is ill-defined and being set to 0.0 in labels with no predicted samples. Use `zero_division` parameter to control this behavior.\n  _warn_prf(average, modifier, f\"{metric.capitalize()} is\", len(result))\n/usr/local/lib/python3.13/dist-packages/sklearn/metrics/_classification.py:1565: UndefinedMetricWarning: Precision is ill-defined and being set to 0.0 in labels with no predicted samples. Use `zero_division` parameter to control this behavior.\n  _warn_prf(average, modifier, f\"{metric.capitalize()} is\", len(result))\n/usr/local/lib/python3.13/dist-packages/sklearn/metrics/_classification.py:1565: UndefinedMetricWarning: Precision is ill-defined and being set to 0.0 in labels with no predicted samples. Use `zero_division` parameter to control this behavior.\n  _warn_prf(average, modifier, f\"{metric.capitalize()} is\", len(result))\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":33},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"***Observations***\n\nThe DummyClassifier achieves an accuracy of approximately 57.06%.\n\nHowever, this result is obtained by always predicting the majority\nclass (target = 0), regardless of the tweet content.\n\nConsequently, the classifier achieves a recall of 1.00 for class 0\nbut fails to identify any disaster-related tweets (class 1).\n\nThis baseline illustrates why accuracy alone is insufficient to\nevaluate a classifier. Precision, recall and F1-score are also\nimportant, particularly for assessing the identification of disaster\ntweets.\n\nMore sophisticated models should be compared against this baseline\nto determine whether they learn useful patterns from the text.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"\n## 5. TF-IDF + Logistic Regression\n\nWe use TF-IDF to represent tweets as numerical features and\nLogistic Regression to classify them as disaster-related or not.\n\nTF-IDF converts text into numerical features that represent the\nimportance of words in each tweet relative to the entire corpus.\nWords that are frequent in a tweet but less common across the\ncorpus tend to receive higher weights.\n\n**Logistic Regression**\n\nLogistic Regression is a supervised learning algorithm used for\nclassification. It learns a relationship between the numerical\nfeatures and the target labels, estimating the probability that\na tweet belongs to each class.\n\n**Model pipeline**\n\nThe two components are combined in a pipeline:\n1. TF-IDF transforms the tweets into numerical feature vectors.\n2. Logistic Regression uses these features to classify tweets\n   as disaster-related (`target = 1`) or not (`target = 0`).\n\nThe model is trained on the training set and evaluated on a\nseparate validation set.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\nfrom sklearn.feature_extraction.text import TfidfVectorizer\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n\n# Define the pipeline\ntext_clf = Pipeline([\n    (\"tfidf\", TfidfVectorizer()),\n    (\"classifier\", LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000))\n])\n\n# Train the model\ntext_clf.fit(X_train, y_train)\n\n# Predict the validation set\ny_pred = text_clf.predict(X_val)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-21T12:40:08.648337Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-21T12:40:08.649236Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-21T12:40:09.825378Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-21T12:40:08.649199Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-21T12:40:09.824705Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":34},{"cell_type":"code","source":"from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score, classification_report\n\nprint(\"Accuracy:\", accuracy_score(y_val, y_pred))\nprint(classification_report(y_val, y_pred))","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-21T12:40:13.840233Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-21T12:40:13.84055Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-21T12:40:13.857476Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-21T12:40:13.840525Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-21T12:40:13.856639Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Accuracy: 0.8069599474720945\n              precision    recall  f1-score   support\n\n           0       0.81      0.87      0.84       869\n           1       0.80      0.73      0.76       654\n\n    accuracy                           0.81      1523\n   macro avg       0.81      0.80      0.80      1523\nweighted avg       0.81      0.81      0.81      1523\n\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":35},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"***Observations***\n\nCompared with the `DummyClassifier` baseline, the model shows a\nsubstantial improvement in classification performance.\n\nUnlike the baseline, which always predicts the majority class,\nthe text classifier identifies disaster-related tweets by learning\npatterns from the training data.\n\nThe results suggest that TF-IDF features combined with Logistic\nRegression provide a useful starting point for this text\nclassification task.\n\nFurther experiments will investigate whether alternative\npreprocessing strategies and model configurations can improve\nperformance.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### 5.1 Confusion Matrix\n\nThe confusion matrix provides a detailed view of the classification\nresults by comparing the true labels with the predicted labels.\n\nIt allows us to identify correct predictions and the two types\nof classification errors:\n- False positives: non-disaster tweets classified as disasters.\n- False negatives: disaster tweets classified as non-disasters.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom sklearn.metrics import ConfusionMatrixDisplay, confusion_matrix\n\ncm = confusion_matrix(y_val, y_pred)\n\ndisp = ConfusionMatrixDisplay(\n    confusion_matrix=cm,\n    display_labels=[\"Not Disaster\", \"Disaster\"]\n)\n\ndisp.plot()\nplt.title(\"Confusion Matrix - TF-IDF + Logistic Regression\")\nplt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-21T12:26:13.682431Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-21T12:26:13.682779Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-21T12:26:13.91812Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-21T12:26:13.682724Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-21T12:26:13.917113Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 640x480 with 2 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":16},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### 5.2 False positives and true negatives\n\nWe examine false positives and false negatives to better understand\nthe limitations of the baseline text classifier.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# False positives: non-disaster tweets predicted as disasters\nfalse_positives = X_val[(y_val == 0) & (y_pred == 1)]\n\n# False negatives: disaster tweets predicted as non-disasters\nfalse_negatives = X_val[(y_val == 1) & (y_pred == 0)]\n\nprint(\"False positives:\")\ndisplay(false_positives.head(10).to_frame(name=\"text\"))\n\nprint(\"False negatives:\")\ndisplay(false_negatives.head(10).to_frame(name=\"text\"))","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-21T12:26:13.919187Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-21T12:26:13.919488Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-21T12:26:13.93602Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-21T12:26:13.919456Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-21T12:26:13.935218Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"False positives:\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"                                                   text\n4863  @TheEconomist Step one: get that mass murderer...\n1358  if firefighters acted like cops they'd drive a...\n2685  Ignition Knock (Detonation) Sensor-Senso Stand...\n5267             @TroySlaby22 slicker than an oil spill\n5119  Has An Ancient Nuclear Reactor Been Discovered...\n809   Article by Michael Jackman at Metro Times Detr...\n4955  DFR EP016 Monthly Meltdown - On Dnbheaven 2015...\n3057  #Sismo M 1.3 - 1km NNE of The Geysers Californ...\n2986                        Drowning in Actavis suicide\n4700  'Since1970the 2 biggest depreciations in CAD:U...","text/html":"<div>\n<style scoped>\n    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n        vertical-align: middle;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n        vertical-align: top;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe thead th {\n        text-align: right;\n    }\n</style>\n<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n      <th></th>\n      <th>text</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <th>4863</th>\n      <td>@TheEconomist Step one: get that mass murderer...</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>1358</th>\n      <td>if firefighters acted like cops they'd drive a...</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\